<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claudia gens</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Claudii</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Claudia gens was one of the great patrician families of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, said to descend from the Sabine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attus-clausus">Attus Clausus</a>, who settled in Rome around 504 BCE. Its members, proud and harsh in Roman tradition, included Appius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> Caecus, builder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appian-way">Via Appia</a>. Through the branch of the Claudii Nerones the family gave Rome the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> and Claudius.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claudia-gens.jpg" alt="Claudia gens" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original version uploaded by User:George Shuklin on 3 June 2008 · CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Tiberius_-_%D0%9F%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82_%D0%A2%D0%B8%D0%B1%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%8F_A54,_1_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
